<Layouts.app flash={@flash}>
  <section id="tidewake-platform" class="space-y-14">
    <div class="relative overflow-hidden rounded-3xl border border-cyan-200/60 bg-slate-950 px-6 py-14 text-white shadow-2xl shadow-cyan-950/20 sm:px-12">
      <div class="absolute -right-20 -top-24 h-64 w-64 rounded-full bg-cyan-400/20 blur-3xl">
      </div>
      <div class="absolute -bottom-32 left-1/4 h-72 w-72 rounded-full bg-blue-500/20 blur-3xl">
      </div>

      <div class="relative max-w-3xl">
        <p class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-full border border-cyan-300/30 bg-cyan-300/10 px-3 py-1 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-cyan-100">
          <span class="size-2 rounded-full bg-cyan-300"></span> Pre-release
        </p>

        <h1 class="mt-7 text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-balance sm:text-6xl">
          Reliable webhook delivery, built for the rough water.
        </h1>

        <p class="mt-6 max-w-2xl text-base leading-8 text-slate-300 sm:text-lg">
          Tidewake is a pre-release platform for reliable webhook delivery: durable event
          ingestion, asynchronous fan-out, signed HTTP requests, and bounded retries.
        </p>

        <div class="mt-9 flex flex-wrap gap-3 text-sm text-slate-200">
          <span class="rounded-full border border-white/15 bg-white/5 px-4 py-2">Phoenix 1.8</span>
          <span class="rounded-full border border-white/15 bg-white/5 px-4 py-2">PostgreSQL</span>
          <span class="rounded-full border border-white/15 bg-white/5 px-4 py-2">Oban</span>
          <span class="rounded-full border border-white/15 bg-white/5 px-4 py-2">Req</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div id="delivery-flow" class="space-y-6">
      <div>
        <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-cyan-700">
          Implemented delivery flow
        </p>
        <h2 class="mt-2 text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-slate-950 dark:text-white">
          One durable path from event to endpoint
        </h2>
      </div>

      <ol class="grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-4">
        <li class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-5 shadow-sm dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-900">
          <span class="text-xs font-bold text-cyan-700 dark:text-cyan-300">01</span>
          <p class="mt-3 font-semibold text-slate-950 dark:text-white">Receive</p>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300">
            Authenticate a service account and accept an event with project-scoped idempotency.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-5 shadow-sm dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-900">
          <span class="text-xs font-bold text-cyan-700 dark:text-cyan-300">02</span>
          <p class="mt-3 font-semibold text-slate-950 dark:text-white">Persist</p>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300">
            Commit the event, deliveries, and initial jobs together in PostgreSQL.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-5 shadow-sm dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-900">
          <span class="text-xs font-bold text-cyan-700 dark:text-cyan-300">03</span>
          <p class="mt-3 font-semibold text-slate-950 dark:text-white">Schedule</p>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300">
            Fan out asynchronously through Oban to active endpoints in the event's project.
          </p>
        </li>
        <li class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-5 shadow-sm dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-900">
          <span class="text-xs font-bold text-cyan-700 dark:text-cyan-300">04</span>
          <p class="mt-3 font-semibold text-slate-950 dark:text-white">Deliver</p>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300">
            Send an HMAC-signed HTTP request, record the outcome, and retry eligible failures.
          </p>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </div>

    <div
      id="current-status"
      class="grid gap-5 rounded-3xl bg-cyan-50 p-6 sm:grid-cols-[1fr_auto] sm:items-center sm:p-8 dark:bg-cyan-950/30"
    >
      <div>
        <h2 class="text-sm font-semibold text-cyan-900 dark:text-cyan-100">
          Implemented and tested
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-2 max-w-2xl leading-7 text-cyan-950/70 dark:text-cyan-100/70">
          Req HTTP delivery includes SSRF destination checks, DNS pinning, and a bounded response
          size. Automatic retries use bounded exponential backoff with jitter. Stale-delivery
          recovery and delivery status reads are implemented, with at-least-once semantics:
          a request may be sent again when its result was not persisted.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-2 max-w-2xl leading-7 text-cyan-950/70 dark:text-cyan-100/70">
          Service accounts provide expiring, revocable credentials, role permissions, and project
          isolation. Admin-only APIs support idempotent manual retry and paginated retry audit
          history. These capabilities have automated regression tests; Telemetry events and domain
          metrics are available.
        </p>
      </div>
      <a
        id="architecture-link"
        href="https://github.com/Carlos-ccaetano/Tidewake/blob/main/docs/architecture.md"
        class="inline-flex items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-cyan-950 px-5 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-white transition hover:-translate-y-0.5 hover:bg-cyan-800 focus:outline-none focus:ring-2 focus:ring-cyan-600 focus:ring-offset-2 dark:bg-cyan-200 dark:text-cyan-950"
      >
        Read the architecture
      </a>
    </div>

    <div id="future-work" class="space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-slate-950 dark:text-white">
        Future work and operational limits
      </h2>
      <p class="max-w-3xl leading-7 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300">
        An operational UI and human authentication remain future work. There is no retry dashboard.
        Respecting Retry-After received from destinations, retention and disposal policies,
        external metrics reporting, and alerts are still pending.
      </p>
      <p class="max-w-3xl leading-7 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300">
        Development and tests use a deterministic adapter by default; local HTTP delivery requires
        explicit configuration. Automated tests do not establish production readiness: no
        production deployment or end-to-end production integration with Ironhold has been proven.
      </p>
      <nav aria-label="Project resources" class="flex flex-wrap gap-3">
        <a
          id="documentation-link"
          href="https://github.com/Carlos-ccaetano/Tidewake/blob/main/README.md"
          class="rounded-lg px-3 py-2 font-semibold text-cyan-700 underline underline-offset-4 focus:outline-none focus:ring-2 focus:ring-cyan-600 dark:text-cyan-300"
        >
          Documentation
        </a>
        <a
          id="roadmap-link"
          href="https://github.com/Carlos-ccaetano/Tidewake/blob/main/docs/roadmap.md"
          class="rounded-lg px-3 py-2 font-semibold text-cyan-700 underline underline-offset-4 focus:outline-none focus:ring-2 focus:ring-cyan-600 dark:text-cyan-300"
        >
          Roadmap
        </a>
        <a
          id="source-link"
          href="https://github.com/Carlos-ccaetano/Tidewake"
          class="rounded-lg px-3 py-2 font-semibold text-cyan-700 underline underline-offset-4 focus:outline-none focus:ring-2 focus:ring-cyan-600 dark:text-cyan-300"
        >
          Source code
        </a>
        <a
          id="ironhold-link"
          href="https://github.com/Carlos-ccaetano/Ironhold"
          class="rounded-lg px-3 py-2 font-semibold text-cyan-700 underline underline-offset-4 focus:outline-none focus:ring-2 focus:ring-cyan-600 dark:text-cyan-300"
        >
          Ironhold companion receiver
        </a>
      </nav>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layouts.app>
